From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 11:08:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] 4927, 4928: each rate limiter counts on its own
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The limiter's bucket key was the window, the cap and the user, nothing
else. So every limiter with the same numbers shared ONE budget per user:
at 30 a minute that is the tasks, updates and requests routers plus five
thread routes, among them /threads/:id/routes and /chain-position. The
app polls, and the list fetches a path per card on screen; together they
run past 30, and the client, as asked, draws no path and no „გზები"
button on a 429. That fits both of Giorgi's FAILs („no path anywhere",
„the routes button is gone").

Now each rateLimit() has its own id in the key: one limiter used on
several routes still counts them together, two limiters never do. No
cap changes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
